Title: POLITICIAN
Credit: written by
Author: Leonard Menchiari
Draft date: 2026-11-10 (shooting script, draft 2)

/* File: stories/politician/screenplay.fountain
   Draft 2: Leonard's 40 PDF comments applied (idea.md), plus fixes that restore his text.
   Shot notes: [[SHOT | seconds | size and angle | movement | note]]. Scene ids S01..S11, shot ids per scene.
   PROPOSED in this draft (his call): the gold bobblehead of himself as the bookend; bearer bonds as the "large document bills"; the final line; the scope with face boxes; the Walther PPK/S.
   Accents: everyone in the town and the news speaks English with strong accents nobody can place. The old man is American, with a slight accent. */

.INT. HIS CAR - MOVING - DAY #S01#

[[SH010 | 2 | EXTREME CLOSE | Locked-off, car vibration | PROPOSED bookend: first and last image of the film]]

A gold bobblehead on a dashboard: a grinning old man in a suit, thumb up, nodding with every bump. A news anchor's voice on the radio. Under it, a roar grows.

SMASH CUT TO:

.EXT. CITIES - VARIOUS - DAY TO SUNSET #S02#

[[SH010 | 3 | WIDE, high | Handheld, phone-camera feel | Riots open the film (Leonard)]]

A crowd fills an avenue from wall to wall. Above the heads, signs with the same old face: devil horns drawn on, the eyes crossed out in red, one printout of him photoshopped hanging from a noose.

NEWS ANCHORS (V.O.)
(overlapping, many accents)
...the index lost another eleven percent... ...fuel up again overnight...

[[SH020 | 2 | INSERT | Locked-off | ]]

A cardboard sign. His face. A red X over each eye.

[[SH030 | 3 | MEDIUM | Locked-off | Numbers per liter, no currency sign: the place stays unplaceable]]

A gas station. A worker on a ladder pulls 1.94 off the price board and slides in 5.89. Under it, DIESEL: 2.07 becomes 6.31. A line of cars behind him. Nobody honks.

[[SH040 | 2 | WIDE, long lens | Locked-off | ]]

A highway out of the city, jammed. Mattresses tied on car roofs. Children's faces at the windows.

[[SH050 | 4 | WIDE, long lens | Handheld | Distance: nothing explicit]]

A police line. Hands pull a POLICEMAN into the crowd by his vest. Another officer drags him back. A pistol rises above the heads and fires. The police fire back. Everyone scatters.

[[SH060 | 3 | MEDIUM WIDE | Handheld | Leonard: riot shields struck]]

A wall of riot shields. A bottle of fire bursts against it. Flames run down the shields and over the boots. The line breaks.

[[SH070 | 3 | WIDE | Locked-off | Leonard: the truck, realistic]]

A police truck stands abandoned, windows smashed. A bottle sails through the broken windshield. Fire fills the cab.

[[SH080 | 2 | EXTREME WIDE | Slow pan | ]]

Sunset. The skyline, columns of smoke, sirens far away.

[[SH090 | 8 | MEDIUM, a TV in a shop window | Locked-off | Leonard: seen on a screen, professional news logos. His clean face on screen]]

A television behind a cracked shop window. A news channel: a polished logo, a red BREAKING bar, a ticker of red numbers. In the corner, his official portrait: the same old face, clean, smiling. A REPORTER, sexy, every hair in place, on a rooftop with smoke behind her.

REPORTER
His location is still unknown. Authorities are warning the locals that any harm to this man will have serious repercussions.

SMASH CUT TO:

.EXT. DIRT ROAD INTO A TOWN - DAY #S03#

[[SH010 | 2 | EXTREME WIDE | Locked-off | Hard cut to silence]]

Silence. The sun on the rooftops of a dry, dusty town.

[[SH020 | 3 | MEDIUM | Locked-off | Leonard: stray dog]]

A stray dog lies in the shadow of an abandoned building, on the edge of a crumbled concrete wall. Heat rises off the ground.

[[SH030 | 3 | EXTREME WIDE, long lens | Locked-off | Leonard: one more shot here]]

Far out on a dirt road, a car comes out of the heat shimmer at full speed, a plume of dust behind it.

[[SH040 | 2 | LOW, ground level | Locked-off, car passes over camera | The speeding car (Leonard)]]

The car tears over the camera.

[[SH050 | 2 | INSERT, ground level | Locked-off | ]]

A front wheel locks and slides through the dirt to a rough stop. Dust rolls past.

The dog lifts its head.

[[SH060 | 5 | MEDIUM, through windshield | Locked-off | ]]

The OLD MAN behind the wheel, American, his shirt dark with sweat, slowly raises his head and looks ahead, frightened. On the dashboard, the gold bobblehead keeps nodding: it is him. On the passenger seat a BRIEFCASE, papers sticking out of it, shut in a hurry.

[[SH070 | 3 | POV | Dolly zoom | Vertigo effect (Leonard)]]

The dirt road runs straight into the town. It stretches away from him.

[[SH080 | 3 | MEDIUM | Two whip pans, left and right | Leonard: no walls, no roads; the only way is through]]

Left: broken ground, a ditch, rubble. No road. Right: the same. The town spreads across the whole horizon. The road goes in.

[[SH090 | 2 | INSERT | Locked-off | ]]

The rear-view mirror. An empty road. Nobody.

[[SH100 | 2 | INSERT | Locked-off | ]]

The fuel needle rests on the edge of E.

[[SH110 | 3 | CLOSE | Locked-off | ]]

Sweat runs down his temple. He breathes in, and gently presses the accelerator.

.EXT. TOWN - MAIN STREET - DAY #S04#

[[SH010 | 5 | WIDE, side view | Tracking parallel, long lens, flat | Leonard: side view like a side-scroller ("Keep Driving")]]

The car crawls across the frame. Behind it, tall cheap apartment blocks slide past: laundry, satellite dishes, shutters half down. Nobody outside. From open windows the same news echoes from television to television.

[[SH020 | 7 | MEDIUM, passenger side | Locked-off | ]]

He glances at the briefcase.

OLD MAN
We'll get there, don't worry... Wait till they see what I was able to-- what--? No, no no no...

The engine pops.

[[SH030 | 2 | GROUND LEVEL | Locked-off | Leonard]]

A front wheel rolls toward the camera and stops right in front of it.

[[SH040 | 4 | EXTREME WIDE, high | Locked-off | Leonard: alone in a large empty crossroads]]

The car sits alone in the middle of a large, empty crossroads. A beep: the fuel light. The keys twist. The car goes quiet. The last clap of the engine echoes off the buildings.

[[SH050 | 4 | MEDIUM CLOSE | Handheld, gentle | ]]

OLD MAN
Not here, no...

He peeks around. Empty. He takes the briefcase and gets out, leaving the door open.

.EXT. TOWN - SIDE STREETS - DAY #S05#

[[SH010 | 3 | MEDIUM | Handheld, tracking beside him | We stay with him (Leonard, Q12)]]

He walks fast, the briefcase against his chest, trying not to make a sound. His breath gets heavier.

[[SH020 | 2 | POV | Handheld | Leonard: the shots of what he checks]]

A doorway. A bead curtain sways.

[[SH030 | 2 | POV | Handheld | ]]

A window. A television glows. An old woman eating turns her head toward the street.

[[SH040 | 3 | MEDIUM WIDE | Handheld | Leonard: he feels recognized and runs]]

On his left, a small group of people at a doorway. One of them looks at him. Looks again. Nudges the man next to him. The old man walks faster. Then he runs.

[[SH050 | 3 | MEDIUM | Handheld | Leonard: bounces and falls]]

He turns a corner and slams into a big, robust FAT PERSON. He bounces off him and lands on the ground.

[[SH060 | 4 | LOW, from the ground | Handheld | Leonard: not sure yet]]

The fat person looks down at him. He can't place him. Then his eyes widen with excitement.

FAT PERSON
(a thick accent from nowhere you could name)
Hey... wait. Aren't you--

[[SH070 | 4 | CLOSE | Handheld | ]]

On the ground, the old man covers his face with his hand.

OLD MAN
I don't know who you think I am. I don't know you!

[[SH080 | 6 | MEDIUM | Handheld | ]]

FAT PERSON
It IS you. What are you doing here, all alone? Nobody around to baby-sit you?

Behind him, his FRIEND raises a phone and films.

[[SH090 | 2 | INSERT, the friend's phone | Locked-off | Leonard: video, then texting. Generic app, no brand]]

The phone screen: a few seconds of video of the old man on the ground. He sends it to a group chat with hundreds of members. Replies start stacking up.

[[SH100 | 4 | CLOSE TWO SHOT | Handheld, tight | ]]

The fat person grabs him by the collar and hauls him up.

FAT PERSON
Is that what you do with our tax money?

[[SH110 | 2 | MEDIUM | Handheld | Leonard: more realistic line]]

FRIEND
(filming)
Hold him! Hold him, I'm filming!

[[SH120 | 6 | CLOSE | Handheld, tight | ]]

FAT PERSON
Give me one reason why I shouldn't rip your guts open right now, in front of everyone.

[[SH130 | 2 | WIDE, low | Locked-off | ]]

Above them, faces appear at the windows.

[[SH140 | 3 | MEDIUM | Handheld | ]]

The old man shrinks and slides out of the grip. The fat person lets him go. The old man runs.

.EXT. TOWN - STREETS TO THE CROSSROADS - CONTINUOUS #S06#

[[SH010 | 3 | MEDIUM | Handheld, backing in front of him | Leonard: variation in the voices]]

He runs. The buildings wake up. Someone bangs a pot on a balcony railing. A whistle. A shutter slams open.

VOICES
(from windows and balconies, overlapping)
Thief! / Close the street! / He's going to the crossroads!

[[SH020 | 3 | WIDE, long lens | Handheld | ]]

Behind him the two friends run, and people pour out of doorways to join them.

[[SH030 | 2 | WIDE | Handheld, running | ]]

A whole crowd runs after him, faster than he is.

[[SH040 | 2 | MEDIUM | Handheld, running | Leonard: he trips]]

He trips. The briefcase hits the asphalt and bursts open.

[[SH050 | 3 | INSERT | Locked-off | PROPOSED: bearer bonds, Leonard's "large document bills". Research item]]

Large engraved certificates spill out: PAY TO BEARER. ONE HUNDRED THOUSAND US DOLLARS.

[[SH060 | 3 | WIDE | Handheld | His decoy (Leonard, Part 1)]]

He looks at the crowd, then flings the open case toward them. The certificates fly. The front of the crowd drops to the ground, fighting over them.

[[SH070 | 3 | CLOSE | Handheld, running | ]]

VOICE (O.S.)
Don't let him get away!!!

He runs on toward the crossroads, pulling out his phone.

[[SH080 | 2 | INSERT, his phone | Locked-off | Leonard: clear insert of the phone]]

His sweaty thumb slides across the lock screen. It fails. It works. A contact with no name, only a number. Call.

[[SH090 | 10 | CLOSE | Handheld, running | ]]

OLD MAN
(into the phone)
It's me! I have the money! The car broke down, I'm on foot, come get me, fast! I'm slightly south from where we were supposed to meet, the add--

[[SH100 | 2 | CLOSE | Handheld | ]]

A rock hits him between the phone and his ear.

[[SH110 | 3 | WIDE | Handheld | ELEMENT from here: old man beaten (Leonard). Not exaggerated: he must still look cool at the end]]

He falls and rolls onto the sidewalk at the corner of the crossroads. Blood runs down his face. The yelling closes in.

.EXT. CROSSROADS - CONTINUOUS #S07#

[[SH010 | 3 | LOW, his eye level on the ground | Handheld | Leonard: the crowd getting closer]]

Feet and faces fill the frame, closing in.

[[SH020 | 4 | MEDIUM, low | Locked-off | Gun: Walther PPK/S, nickel, 7 in the magazine plus 1 chambered = 8 (PROPOSED model, capacity checked)]]

A gunshot. Everyone freezes. On the ground, he holds a small nickel pistol up at the sky.

OLD MAN
STAY BACK!!!

[[SH030 | 4 | MEDIUM | Handheld | ]]

He points it at the crowd. They take a step back.

OLD MAN
Don't get close! Go away!

[[SH040 | 4 | WIDE | Slow push in | ]]

Some of them back away. The tough ones step forward. They don't run. They walk toward him, slowly, without fear.

[[SH050 | 7 | MEDIUM, his side | Handheld | Countdown (Leonard). The warning shot is not in his count. Distance on the falls]]

He shoots. A man drops. He shoots again. Another drops. The rest break into a sprint. He keeps firing, counting down under his breath.

OLD MAN
...four... three... two...

[[SH060 | 3 | CLOSE | Locked-off | ]]

He fires once more.

OLD MAN
One.

He stops.

[[SH070 | 6 | CLOSE, slow push in | Locked-off | Leonard: more intense, the realization]]

Running feet behind him. He looks at them. He looks at the gun. His breathing slows. He won't give them this. He presses the muzzle to his temple and closes his eyes.

[[SH080 | 2 | EXTREME CLOSE | Locked-off | ]]

Click.

[[SH090 | 3 | CLOSE | Locked-off | ]]

He opens his eyes. Looks at the gun. Then up, at the sky, where his first bullet went. The crowd hits him.

.EXT. CROSSROADS - MOMENTS LATER #S08#

[[SH010 | 3 | EXTREME WIDE, high | Locked-off | Seen from afar (Leonard). Read later as the helicopter's view? Decide]]

From far above, the small mob closes around him. He disappears inside it. Fists and kicks rise and fall.

[[SH020 | 3 | MEDIUM | Handheld | Leonard: rope thrown over the light]]

A rope sails over the arm of a street light at the corner.

[[SH030 | 3 | WIDE | Locked-off | ]]

They haul him up by the ankles, upside down.

[[SH040 | 3 | CLOSE, upside down | Locked-off | Not exaggerated (Leonard)]]

His face: bruised, a split lip, blood from his ear. With effort, he opens one eye.

[[SH050 | 3 | POV, upside down | Locked-off | A swing or two (Leonard). Impact on the body]]

A man swings a metal pipe into his body. Again.

[[SH060 | 2 | LOW, looking up | Locked-off | Leonard: from below]]

The pipe rises high against the sky for the last blow.

[[SH070 | 2 | HIGH, from above | Locked-off | Leonard: the sniper hits him in the face, seen from above: nothing explicit]]

A crack from the sky. The man's head snaps back. He drops. The pipe rings on the asphalt.

[[SH080 | 3 | WIDE | Locked-off | Leonard: wide of the crowd stepping back. Method: AI crowd first, simulation only if it fails]]

The crowd steps back from the body, looking up.

.EXT. SKY ABOVE THE TOWN / INT. HELICOPTER - CONTINUOUS #S09#

[[SH010 | 3 | EXTREME WIDE, long lens | Locked-off | Tone shift: Clancy, hint of Kojima (Leonard, Q12). Fancy VIP model: research]]

A fancy helicopter, glossy, a private VIP machine, holds still high above the rooftops. The side door open.

[[SH020 | 3 | CLOSE | Locked-off, cabin vibration | ]]

In the door, between cream leather seats, ROGER, harnessed in, cheek on the stock of a long rifle. He is smiling.

[[SH030 | 4 | SCOPE POV | Steady, stabilized | PROPOSED: the tech that exists but nobody sees]]

The crossroads through his scope. A thin box frames every face: red. One box, upside down under the street light, is green. The crosshair moves from red box to red box.

[[SH040 | 4 | WIDE, from the street, long lens | Locked-off | Distance and dust: nothing explicit]]

Cracks from the sky. People fall. The rest run. Some fall while they run.

[[SH050 | 3 | MEDIUM | Locked-off | ]]

Behind Roger, seated, immaculate, a headset over her hair: the BUSINESS LADY.

BUSINESS LADY
That's enough Roger.

[[SH060 | 3 | CLOSE | Locked-off | ]]

Roger's face, for an instant: a child whose candy was taken. Then his face goes blank. He shifts his aim.

[[SH070 | 2 | SCOPE POV | Steady | ]]

The crosshair settles on the rope. A crack.

[[SH080 | 2 | WIDE | Locked-off | ]]

The rope snaps.

.EXT. CROSSROADS - CONTINUOUS #S10#

[[SH010 | 5 | MEDIUM | Handheld | Leonard: specify]]

He drops onto the asphalt shoulder first and screams.

OLD MAN
Fuck! FUCK! Fuck fuck fuck...

He curls up, shaking. A dark stain spreads down his trousers.

[[SH020 | 3 | HIS POV | Handheld | ]]

The dead lie around him, certificates stuck to the asphalt between them.

[[SH030 | 5 | MEDIUM, low, his eye height | Locked-off | Leonard: lying back like on a couch, taking it like a champ]]

He rolls onto his back and lies on the sidewalk as if it were a couch, legs out on the street. He catches his breath. He looks at the sky. Nearly a smile.

[[SH040 | 3 | MEDIUM | Locked-off | ]]

He turns his head and spits on the nearest body.

[[SH050 | 6 | LOW ANGLE, briefcase in the foreground | Locked-off | Leonard: the helicopter lands behind him as he reaches the case]]

The open briefcase lies near the camera. Behind it he gets up and limps toward it. Behind him the helicopter comes down into the crossroads, the rotor wash blowing the certificates across the bodies. He reaches the case.

[[SH060 | 3 | INSERT | Locked-off | ]]

He reaches into the pocket inside the lid and takes out a folder.

[[SH070 | 3 | WIDE | Locked-off | ]]

The BUSINESS LADY steps out, low under the rotors, and walks to him.

[[SH080 | 5 | MEDIUM | Locked-off | His line (Leonard)]]

OLD MAN
What took you so long? I don't pay your ass for nothing.

[[SH090 | 4 | TWO SHOT | Locked-off | Her silence answers him]]

She doesn't answer. She holds out her hand. He gives her the folder. She opens it to the last page.

[[SH100 | 2 | INSERT, the last page | Locked-off | Leonard: readable on pause, clear signature. PROP: the Agreement (last page of this PDF)]]

Dense clauses. At the bottom, his signature, large and clear.

[[SH110 | 5 | CLOSE | Locked-off | Final line: PROPOSED (Leonard asked for one)]]

She closes the folder. She looks at the bodies, then at him.

BUSINESS LADY
Now that it's signed... there's no one left to hang.

[[SH120 | 3 | MEDIUM | Locked-off | ]]

He looks at her. She turns and walks back to the helicopter. He follows her in.

.INT. HIS CAR - CROSSROADS - CONTINUOUS #S11#

[[SH010 | 10 | MEDIUM, through the windshield | Locked-off | PROPOSED bookend: same bobblehead as the first image. The helicopter going away (Leonard)]]

The gold bobblehead in the foreground, nodding hard in the rotor wash. Through the windshield the helicopter lifts off, banks over the rooftops and goes away into the sky. The bobblehead slows. Keeps nodding. The sky is empty.

> CUT TO BLACK.
